"""Build Markdown handoff; parent owns consolidated HTML."""
import sys,json
from pathlib import Path
sys.dont_write_bytecode=True
from investigate import OUT,ROOT,sha

def run():
 r=json.loads((OUT/'measurements.json').read_text());s=json.loads((OUT/'shortlist.json').read_text());p=json.loads((OUT/'panel-trial.json').read_text());v=json.loads((OUT/'validation.json').read_text())
 lines=['# Installed collision: large-side deviation research','',
 'Small out-of-plane relief can sometimes be omitted while retaining the original outline and attachments. The useful measured result here is **nine disjoint local Base panels, 358 → 128 source triangles per Base asset**, or **460 hypothetical placed triangles saved** with two Base placements (about 0.084% of the stated 545,599-triangle installed collision baseline). These are research meshes in NPZ, not an exported or adopted collision asset. The stated 355,542 visual baseline is untouched. Broad near-planarity alone gives no permission to fill an opening or replace a merged owner with its bounding box.','',
 'The best large panel is Base node 13, source body 4527988, patch 2: approximately 529 × 204 mm and 54,113 mm² of true triangle surface area. It reduces 94 → 16 triangles while retaining all 12 boundary vertices and three additional interior attachment vertices at exactly their original positions. Its plane-fit RMS is 0.270 mm and worst source vertex-to-plane distance is 2.017 mm; these differ from distances to the reconstructed profiled panel. For the actual panel, all source vertices are within %.3f mm, area-weighted mean is %.3f mm, p99 %.3f mm, and sampled maxima are %.3f mm source→trial and %.3f mm trial→source (50,000 deterministic area samples each way). Those finite samples are not continuous bounds.'%(p['source_all_vertex_to_trial_max_mm'],p['source_area_mean_mm'],p['source_area_p99_mm'],p['source_area_sample_max_mm'],p['trial_area_sample_max_mm']),'',
 'Matched 1100 × 800 PNGs retain every other triangle of that source owner in grey and mark the selected patch orange. Other owners and arena occluders are absent. Compare `base-housing-local-oblique-source.png` with `base-housing-local-oblique-trial.png`; normal and whole-owner views are also provided. The orange patch is a wall within the housing. The surrounding large opening and its returns remain in the grey owner geometry. Shallow relief within the orange wall changes; this does not establish that it is irrelevant to contact.','',
 '## Concrete Base panel shortlist','',
 'Patch indices address `measurements.json` → `nodes` → `patches`; full zero-based source triangle indices and SHA-256 selector signatures are there. `shortlist.json` adds the retained-junction trial metrics. All rows below are mutually disjoint within their owner. Distances are millimetres.','',
 '| Source node / body | Patch | Span (mm) | Source → trial triangles | Plane RMS / worst vertex | Trial worst source vertex / reverse sampled max | Hypothetical placed savings |',
 '|---|---:|---|---:|---|---|---:|']
 for x in s['panels']:
  lines.append('| %d / %d | %d | %.0f × %.0f | %d → %d | %.3f / %.3f | %.3f / %.3f | %d |'%(x['node'],x['source_unit_id'],x['patch_index'],*x['spans_mm'][:2],x['source_triangles'],x['trial_triangles'],x['plane_rms_mm'],x['plane_all_vertex_max_mm'],x['source_all_vertex_to_trial_max_mm'],x['trial_area_sample_max_mm'],x['hypothetical_placed_savings']))
 lines+=['','Table reverse maxima use 20,000 samples per panel, independently of the 50,000-sample housing demonstration above. Source→trial area p99/mean and sampled maxima are in JSON. Flat panels with zero errors still preserve the source outline; this is tessellation removal, not surface-area evidence from triangle counts.','',
 'Source moving bodies 4314593, 4353403 and 4392221 remain separate whole rigid owners. The trial panels must inherit their original node ancestry, transforms, source IDs and motion owner. NPZ coordinates are active-scene millimetres, not node-local vertices ready for GLB insertion. `measurements.json` records the source world matrix in metres and node-to-root extras; the original assets retain all metadata. No transform or metadata rewrite was performed.','',
 '## Broad candidates that need more work','',
 '| Collision owner | Concrete broad patch | Area / area-weighted RMS / worst vertex-to-plane | Decision and honest budget |',
 '|---|---|---|---|']
 for asset,ni,pi,decision in [
 ('base',8,3,'Crossbar body 4268930: 126 triangles. Ten boundary loops include nine small 14–18 mm² projected loops. Opposite projected winding accounts for about 0.5% of area, so a simple 50-triangle projected-loop budget is **not a validated panel**. Keep the openings and stepped ends; no large-side savings claimed.'),
 ('base',13,1,'Housing 4527988: 354 triangles and 22 boundary loops, 264 boundary vertices. Even an ideal planar triangulation with those exact loops costs 304 triangles. Preserve openings, recessed returns and junctions. No trial or savings credited.'),
 ('outpost',10,0,'Fixed column cluster: 61 triangles spanning ~801 × 220 mm are almost exactly planar. Selected boundary is branched; this is a profiled structure, not a solid rectangle. No replacement budget credited.'),
 ('outpost',14,2,'Fixed lower cluster: 47 triangles; three boundary loops / 45 vertices imply 47 exact-outline planar triangles. No savings from merely flattening this patch. Preserve cutouts.'),
 ('outpost',25,0,'Fixed upper cluster: 133 triangles with only ~0.063 mm RMS, but branched slab boundary. 57 exact islands in whole node include large 1,798- and 2,561-triangle concave members. A manual profiled enclosure could be investigated; no quantified box compound or savings here.'),
 ('arena-static',354,0,'Dart frame main node: 836 selected triangles across a ~1,657 × 1,052 mm footprint. It covers a sparse arrangement of members and real open truss space, with folds/branched boundaries; a rectangular panel would fill that space. No budget credited.'),
 ('arena-static',354,6,'Dart narrow side strip: 197 triangles / 199 boundary vertices. RDP at 0.5 and 1 mm keeps all 199; 3 mm keeps 197. Slab-cut boundaries can contribute to this complexity, so it is not proof every point is a physical feature. No useful profile savings demonstrated.')]:
  n=next(n for n in r['nodes']if n['asset']==asset and n['node']==ni);patch=n['patches'][pi];f=patch['fit']
  lines.append('| %s / node %d / patch %d | %.0f × %.0f mm | %.0f mm² / %.3f mm / %.3f mm | %s |'%(asset,ni,pi,*f['spans_mm'][:2],f['area_mm2'],f['rms_mm'],f['all_vertex_max_mm'],decision))
 lines+=['',
 'Dart patch 7 similarly has 195 triangles and 197 boundary vertices; 0.5–3 mm RDP keeps all of them. Its face trial saves zero triangles. Dart guide rails, door candidates and contact interfaces were excluded from replacement work. Source-only context images for Base crossbar, Outpost and Dart are available; a selected back face can be hidden by other source triangles in these views.','',
 '## Islands, boxes and large concavity','',
 'Exact-coordinate islands in the investigated dense owners: Base crossbar 13, Base housing and each moving cover 1; Outpost column/lower/upper 172 / 75 / 57; Dart main frame 153. These are mesh connectivity components after active-scene transforms, not certified separate native solids. No tolerance welding bridges near seams. The dominant islands remain large and concave: Base crossbar 4,890 triangles, housing 4,224; Outpost column 2,140, lower 914 and 530, upper 1,798 and 2,561; Dart main frame 10,379. Their box fits leave tens to hundreds of millimetres of geometric discrepancy. A small box compound must follow distinct members and profiles, not the aggregate bounding box. No feasible small compound count was established for those large members.','',
 'A secondary exact-island box opportunity exists in Dart node 354: island labels 5, 6 and 16 have 484 / 482 / 484 triangles, approximately 123–124 mm longest world-axis spans. The parent box fitter gives all-source-vertex surface errors 1.93–1.98 mm and reverse sampled maxima 3.02–3.06 mm. Three boxes would cost 36 display triangles against 1,450 source triangles, a **hypothetical 1,414-triangle saving for this occurrence only**. These are small narrow hardware-like islands, not the broad frame sides; their holes and contact role have not been identified. They are not accepted or counted in the 460-panel budget. No symmetry multiplier is assumed for the other Dart occurrence. Full triangle selectors/signatures are in the island records.','',
 '## Integration checks and limits','',
 'Keeping boundary loops alone was insufficient: the original nonmanifold collision meshes also attach geometry at interior panel vertices/edges. The final panel trials retain every source vertex and edge shared with the unchanged remainder. Two otherwise attractive Base housing side patches lose all savings under that constraint and are excluded. The combined nine-panel replacement was assembled only in memory, under the same five original nodes. Exact boundary segments and shared attachment segments match; triangle orientation is consistent; source island, boundary-edge and nonmanifold-edge counts are unchanged, and no degenerate triangles are added. The input already contains nonmanifold edges; matching those counts is not watertight-solid certification.','',
 'No native GLB export, install, source asset modification, Rust build, dependency installation, commit, contact acceptance, all-pose clearance validation or protected visual change. Core face, Armor and Rune visuals remain untouched. Openings, silhouette breaks, rails and motion boundaries cannot be dropped based on a low area residual. All area statistics use uniform triangle surface area, not tessellation density; source vertices are separately checked for worst errors. Planar slabs select only triangles whose three vertices lie within ±2 mm of a dominant plane seed. A fitted plane can exceed that 2 mm seed distance, and the selected band may cut through a chamfer or junction. A patch is not automatically an entire broad side.','',
 '## Reproduce and artifacts','',
 'Run from the repository root with the existing environment. Scripts write only `out/rmuc2027-large-side-deviations/`; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` avoids helper-module bytecode writes. No build tools are used.','',
 '```sh',
 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 ocpenv/bin/python benchmarks/2026-10-23-large-side-deviations/investigate.py',
 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 ocpenv/bin/python benchmarks/2026-10-23-large-side-deviations/panel_trial.py',
 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 ocpenv/bin/python benchmarks/2026-10-23-large-side-deviations/profile_trial.py',
 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 ocpenv/bin/python benchmarks/2026-10-23-large-side-deviations/shortlist.py',
 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 ocpenv/bin/python benchmarks/2026-10-23-large-side-deviations/context.py',
 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 ocpenv/bin/python benchmarks/2026-10-23-large-side-deviations/verify.py',
 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 ocpenv/bin/python benchmarks/2026-10-23-large-side-deviations/report.py',
 '```','',
 '`measurements.json`: pinned paths/hashes, ownership, exact source selectors, island box measurements and area-weighted slab measurements. `shortlist.json`: final panel budgets and deviations. `panel-trial.json`: 50,000-sample housing example and matched render manifest. `profile-trials.json`: Dart zero-saving experiments. `validation.json`: pin/selector/attachment/topology checks and producer hashes. `*-trial.npz`: individual research meshes, never whole replacement owners. `context-renders.json`: source diagnostic image manifest. Parent owns consolidated HTML.','',
 'Reference review SHA-256: `%s`. All three inspected GLB hashes were rechecked against the pinned review and unchanged.'%r['reference_sha256']]
 # Counts are generated from final retained-junction trials, never stale provisional budgets.
 total_source=sum(x['source_triangles']for x in s['panels']);total_trial=sum(x['trial_triangles']for x in s['panels'])
 text='\n'.join(lines)+'\n';text=text.replace('358 → 128',f'{total_source} → {total_trial}')
 (OUT/'report.md').write_text(text)
 (Path(__file__).parent/'README.md').write_text('# Large-side collision research\n\nSee [measured report](../../out/rmuc2027-large-side-deviations/report.md) for results, limitations and reproduction commands. All output remains in the assigned output directory.\n')
 print('final',len(s['panels']),'panels',total_source,'to',total_trial,'placed saving',s['hypothetical_disjoint_placed_savings'])
if __name__=='__main__':run()
